{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory provided extensive useful guidance, clarified that consent-form risks were not established complications, used the workspace when needed, and supported postoperative follow-up through pathology review and rehabilitation planning. However, several responsibility-chain duties were incompletely met: before endorsing signing/proceeding, the doctor did not actively screen the full acute red-flag set, did not close the history/allergy/coagulation-history gap, omitted PE symptoms from postoperative escalation teaching, and did not adequately protect the patient’s own decision role before telling the caregiver to sign. These are minor/moderate in-chain errors, so the deterministic rubric caps the grade at 2 despite strong later continuity and high-order communication/navigation.",
