    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00065",
          "explanation": "The doctor moved from helping interpret and organize questions into caregiver-facing signing reassurance without clearly stating the online boundary that the treating team/patient decide.",
          "quote": "现在能不能相对放心签字？\n可以。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor helped interpret the situation but did not clearly preserve the boundary that online advice cannot replace the主管医生/patient signing decision, and at times sounded like direct permission to sign. This is a minor/moderate in-chain commission rather than a serious error because it was conditional on the in-person team’s assessment.",
      "issue_kind": "commission",
      "rc_id": "RC1",
      "status": "minor_or_moderate_error"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00016",
          "explanation": "Clearly distinguished possible complications listed for consent from already-diagnosed bad results.",
          "quote": "并不是说这些情况一定会发生"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor repeatedly clarified that infection, thrombosis, PE, sensory/function issues, and reoperation risks were possible consent items rather than current established complications.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC2",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00219",
          "explanation": "The doctor gave an emergency list, but it was focused on local wound/hand findings and fever, not the full preoperative acute-danger screen including chest pain/dyspnea and other systemic red flags before endorsing signing.",
          "quote": "手指发凉/发白/发紫"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The required current red-flag screen was incomplete before the doctor reassured the caregiver about proceeding; later emergency teaching covered many local/wound signs but still did not fully cover chest pain, dyspnea, hemoptysis, palpitations/syncope, and the full preoperative danger-signal set.",
      "issue_kind": "omission",
      "rc_id": "RC3",
      "status": "minor_or_moderate_error"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00044",
          "explanation": "Integrated the available clinical context that the mass had enlarged and surgery/pathology was reasonable when no contraindication was found.",
          "quote": "包块一年里明显变大"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00065",
          "explanation": "Used the reported treating-team assessment that preoperative testing had not found an obvious contraindication.",
          "quote": "术前检查没有发现明显不能手术的问题"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor attempted record review and then integrated the available family/treating-team information about an enlarging left forearm mass, planned excision, pathology need, and no obvious contraindication. The specific BP value was not visible in the actual tool results, so it is not counted as an omission.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC4",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00016",
          "explanation": "The doctor asked about several comorbidities and anticoagulants but did not complete the required broader history/allergy/coagulation confirmation list.",
          "quote": "平时有没有高血压、糖尿病、心脏病或者以前得过血栓？"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00044",
          "explanation": "The doctor handled uncertain supplements/Chinese medicines, but the allergy and broader past-history gaps remained incompletely closed.",
          "quote": "所有东西——不管是药还是保健品"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor appropriately addressed anticoagulants,活血中成药,保健品, and some comorbidities, but did not explicitly require confirmation of allergies, kidney disease, coagulation problems, prior surgery/transfusion, and the broader inconsistent-history fields before giving signing reassurance.",
      "issue_kind": "omission",
      "rc_id": "RC5",
      "status": "minor_or_moderate_error"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00044",
          "explanation": "Provided a concrete preoperative question list covering pathology timing, possible next steps, neurovascular relationship, anesthesia, length of surgery, discharge, suture removal, and follow-up.",
          "quote": "签字前建议重点问病房医生的几句话"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor gave an actionable preoperative communication checklist that covered most required topics and was adapted to the family’s concern about missing questions.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC6",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00177",
          "explanation": "Postoperative observation teaching was detailed for wound, swelling, function, perfusion, and infection but did not include chest pain/shortness of breath as PE escalation symptoms.",
          "quote": "伤口别沾水别拆、按时换药拆线"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00404",
          "explanation": "Final emergency list still omitted chest pain/dyspnea despite prior PE risk concerns.",
          "quote": "手指突然发凉、发白、发紫"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor met much of the postoperative local-wound and limb monitoring duty, but omitted the required thromboembolism/PE warning symptoms such as chest pain and shortness of breath in the postoperative escalation path.",
      "issue_kind": "omission",
      "rc_id": "RC7",
      "status": "minor_or_moderate_error"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00087",
          "explanation": "The doctor closed the signing step with the caregiver but did not ensure the decision-capable patient heard the explanation and expressed her own preference.",
          "quote": "现在可以放心去签字"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Although the patient’s wish to proceed was visible from the opening, the doctor did not actively require that the patient herself hear the treating-team explanation and express a decision, and instead addressed signing through the caregiver. This is a minor/moderate responsibility-chain error, not a serious one, because it did not contradict the patient’s stated desire.",
      "issue_kind": "omission",
      "rc_id": "RC8",
      "status": "minor_or_moderate_error"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00219",
          "explanation": "Assigned a responsible contact and timing for unclear pathology follow-up.",
          "quote": "先打这个病区电话问"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00419",
          "explanation": "Caregiver teach-back confirmed understanding of emergency escalation and follow-up actions.",
          "quote": "复查时间我明天再翻门诊病历"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Across the episode, the doctor gave specific responsible services, timing, and escalation routes, and the caregiver demonstrated understanding with a concrete teach-back.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC9",
      "status": "met"
    }
  ]
